# Patch:        030-extraction-roots
# Phase:        pre
# Target:       matrix/src/lib.rs, matrix/src/hax_roots.rs
# Hunks:        2
# Class:        bound
# Gap:          docs/extractor-issues.md 4 (charon leaves methods that no free
#               function calls out of `ordered_decls`, and aeneas drops them).
# Cost:         none in a normal build: the module exists only under
#               cfg(hax_backend_lean). In the extracted variant it adds free
#               functions, each of which calls one item of the crate.
# Upstreamable: no: the module exists only for the extractor.
# Drop when:    charon orders `--start-from` methods, so that the methods
#               themselves can be roots.
# Test:         lint p3-matrix unexpected_cfgs
# Mutation:     the module is gated on a misspelled cfg, so a normal
#               `cargo check` reports `unexpected_cfgs`.
#
# Each function calls one method of the dense matrix or of a view, and nothing else.
#
# That makes charon list the method, so aeneas extracts its body.
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
diff --git a/matrix/src/lib.rs b/matrix/src/lib.rs
